======================================================================
PG1-O00094 MOLECULAR DOCKING — COMPLETE FINAL LOG
======================================================================

Project focus
-------------
Preliminary molecular docking of four apple-associated bioactive
compounds against the modeled PG1 endopolygalacturonase of
Fusarium oxysporum f. sp. lycopersici (UniProt O00094).

Compounds
---------
1. Quercetin
2. Phlorizin
3. Chlorogenic acid
4. Procyanidin B2

Docking software
----------------
AutoDock Vina

Receptor used
-------------
items\Proteins\PG1-O00094\receptor.pdbqt

Ligands used
------------
items\Ligands\pdbqt structure\quercetin.pdbqt
items\Ligands\pdbqt structure\phlorizin.pdbqt
items\Ligands\pdbqt structure\chlorogenic_acid.pdbqt
items\Ligands\pdbqt structure\procyanidin_B2.pdbqt

======================================================================
1. DOCKING PROTOCOL
======================================================================

Initial Quercetin training run
------------------------------
Grid center:
    X = -8.6
    Y =  4.0
    Z = 43.7

Grid size:
    22 x 22 x 24 Angstrom

Focused comparison protocol
----------------------------
The final four-compound comparison used the focused active-site
grid:

    center_x = -9.25
    center_y = -0.10
    center_z = 42.01

    size_x = 20
    size_y = 18
    size_z = 22 Angstrom

Search settings used for the focused comparison:

    exhaustiveness = 16
    num_modes      = 10
    energy_range   = 4

The same receptor, search box, and Vina settings were used for
Quercetin, Phlorizin, Chlorogenic acid, and Procyanidin B2 in the
final comparison.

